e dialogue or music.\n\ndetailed_description:\nNo subtitles, captions, or on-screen dialogue text. Dialogue is spoken audio only.\nAt 0.917s, the new content follows the opening composition from <Picture 1>. The interval before 0.917s is continuation guidance only, with no new dialogue. All new content ends by 5.917s; later alignment frames only hold the final state.\n\n[Shot 1] 0.917s–5.917s. Medium shot inside the underground shelter, matching the scene in <Subject 1>. <Subject 3> stands and looks down at <Subject 2>, who is seated behind a makeshift table covered in blueprints. As <Subject 3> speaks, he makes a calm, slight gesture with his hand. In the background, workers continue to move boxes and organize shelves. The lighting is cool and practical, with a city view visible through a window on the left. Speaking begins immediately in the new content; gestures and gaze changes happen concurrently, without a silent preamble. Natural speech, never accelerated. From 1.017s to 5.267s, <Subject 3> (S1) says <d>[Chinese] 先把人住的地方做好。装修以后再说。</d>. After the final complete word, allow a natural release and hold through 5.917s; the sentence must not spill into alignment frames.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nAmbient sound of a construction site with distant worker chatter and the shuffling of materials, overlaid with a clear, calm male voice. Spoken dialogue and natural ambience only.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
